es  properly and then the truck  unfortunately  slide down the slope and then ran into  the  railway and then at the at around the  same time the train was trying to enter  into the tunnel and then so  the truck hit the head of the car a  where the conductor's room was  there and then uh that caused the whole  train to the rail in the end and then  caused one of the deadliest uh  accident in decades in taiwan and right  now we also know that unfortunately  the conductor is confirmed dead as one  of the 36 people  and uh information showed that he just  recently got married  so this is yet another very very  disastrous and very sad story that we  are seeing here right now today in  taiwan  that is so heartbreaking william and i  think we're probably going to get to  learn  some more of those stories um you  mentioned the current death toll  is that expected to rise  yes unfortunately i think that number  could be going up more  as more of the very seriously injured  passengers  are still being treated in nearby  hospitals and a lot of them uh have  injuries that could uh threaten their  lives later on  so the next few hours will be very  critical and i think the numbers  could go up over the next few hours dws  william yang  joining us from taiwan and william will  continue to check in with you thanks for  your reporting  thank you  you
 

